cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AXIO PREDICT in your research or clinical workflow, please cite it as below."
title: "AXIO PREDICT: A Desktop Application for Lung Cancer Risk Prediction from Low-Dose CT Scans"
version: 2.0.1
date-released: 2026-05-05
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/godsonj64/AXIOPREDICT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/godsonj64/AXIOPREDICT"
abstract: >
  AXIO PREDICT is a cross-platform desktop application that wraps the Sybil v1.6.0
  deep learning model for lung cancer risk prediction from low-dose CT (LDCT) scans.
  It provides a graphical interface for loading DICOM or PNG series, running the
  Sybil ensemble model, visualising attention maps, and an audit toolkit for
  proxy attention diagnostics informed by the 2026 Sybil auditing literature.
keywords:
  - lung cancer
  - risk prediction
  - low-dose CT
  - LDCT
  - DICOM
  - deep learning
  - medical imaging
  - Sybil
  - electron
  - desktop application
  - attention maps
  - clinical decision support
